label announcement
[signal arg="bg:training_hall"]
Amir: Joint class, Thursday. Monster Hunting.
Amir: Private forest, low and mid-tier game only, and yes, before anyone asks, that still means something can kill you if you're careless.
Amir: Parties of up to three. Any department.
Amir: You'll be graded as a group, which means the group you pick matters more than anything you'll do in there.
Amir: You have until Wednesday to sort yourselves. After that, I sort you, and you will not enjoy my version.
Lan (Sus): (Monster Hunting. Private forest. First joint class of the year.)
Lan (Sus): (This is the flag where the story sends killers after both royal heirs at once, dressed up so each country looks like it struck the other first.)
Lan (Sus): (In every playthrough, the protagonist was standing in that forest, because I steered him there myself.)
Lan (Sus): (This time there's nobody standing there but me.)
Lan (Sus): (Then I need people with me who won't fall apart when it happens.)
[signal arg="freetime:ch04"]
label veldero_offer
Lan (Talk): Party up with me. You, me, and whoever else we can talk into it.
Veldero: I would, honestly, but I already told someone I'd be with them. I made the promise before you even asked.
- Ask who he promised
	Lan (Talk): Who did you promise?
	Veldero: You'll see Thursday. Sorry. Bad timing.
- Let it go
	Lan (Default): No, it's fine. Good luck with whoever it is.
	Veldero: Thanks. Really.
Enriko: Party up? Obviously. Who's our third?
Lan (Default): Working on it.
Enriko: Excellent. I trust you completely and have no further questions. So anyway, the shoe[pause=0.35][lspeed=0.25!]...[lspeed]
set {aff_enriko} += 1
label liesel
[signal arg="bg:library_corner"]
He found her in the far corner of the library, the one nobody used because the lamp there had a permanent flicker.
Dark gray hair, dark blue eyes with a flat, assessing sharpness,
a cold set to her mouth that made her look one bad mood away from performing an autopsy on whoever annoyed her.
Liesel (Flat): You're staring.
Lan (Talk): I am.
He sat down across from her without being invited.
Liesel (Flat): Can I help you.
Lan (Default): I need a healer for the monster hunting class.
Liesel (Flat): You and every other first-year in the Physical Department. I've had four requests already this week. I turned down all four.
Lan (Talk): Why?
Liesel (Flat): Because they wanted a shield with a heartbeat. Someone to point at when the monster's about to bite them.
Liesel (Flat): Nobody asked what I actually want out of it. So, which one are you.
label pitch
- "Neither, I hope."
	Lan (Talk): Neither, I hope.
- "Does it matter? You've already decided."
	Lan (Smug): Does it matter which? You've already decided I'm one of them.
	Liesel (Flat): Then change my mind.
	Lan (Talk): Neither, I hope.
set {aff_liesel} += 2
Lan (Talk): I watched your gi output in the practical drills. Smoothest control in the first year, noble or not.
Lan (Talk): You don't waste a drop showing off, which means you'll still have plenty when everyone else has burned through theirs and started panicking.
Lan (Default): I don't need someone to protect. I need someone I don't have to worry about.
Liesel (Flat): That's a nice speech. Anyone can make a nice speech.
Lan (Default): I'm aware.
Liesel (Flat): So prove it. In the forest, when it matters, not in a library where it costs you nothing to sound sincere.
Liesel (Default): You're the first one who asked instead of assumed. That's worth something. Not a yes. Something.
label ginger
He came back two days later, not to ask again,
but because the flickering lamp corner had started to feel less like her territory and more like a place he was simply allowed to be.
Lan (Smile): Peace offering. Dried ginger candy. Settles the stomach after a long cast.
Liesel (Smile): You're trying to be charming.
Lan (Smug): I'm trying to be tolerable. Charming felt like overreaching.
Lan (Default): That the anatomy text you use for the healing diagrams? Less wasted gi if you know exactly what you're fixing instead of flooding the area and hoping.
Liesel (Default): That's the theory, yes. Most people your rank don't know that's the theory.
Lan (Talk): I pay attention.
She didn't send him away. When he pulled a book off the shelf and read across from her in comfortable silence, she didn't object to that either.
set {aff_liesel} += 1
label thursday
[signal arg="bg:private_forest_edge"]
Thursday morning the first-years gathered at the edge of the private forest in their sorted groups.
Veldero stood between Florentine, arms crossed, and Luna, who stood a full pace apart with the posture of someone placed there against her will.
Enriko: Huh. That's a combination.
Veldero: Told you you'd see. Florentine needed a party and I'd already said I'd back her up.
Veldero: Then Luna got assigned in because the sheet ran out of room everywhere else.
Luna (Serious): I did not get assigned. I was placed. There's a difference. I'm noting it for the record.
Veldero: Duly noted.
Florentine (Flirt): Try not to die first, so we can properly enjoy it when you do.
Amir walked twenty-eight parties to the tree line himself.
Amir: Stay with your party. Track, don't chase.
Amir: If something is too big for the three of you, that is information, not an insult. You retreat and you send up a flare.
Amir: I would rather fail all of you than bury one of you.
Enriko: What is that, actually? I've asked around. Nobody's seen a blade shaped like it.
Lan (Default): A montante. Two-handed. Long reach, built for keeping several people at a distance instead of trading blows with one.
Liesel (Flat): That isn't one of the seven styles. Amir didn't mention it.
Lan (Smug): It isn't. I had it made by a traveling smith. My hands took to it better than anything I was actually taught.
Lan (Smug): Nobody around uses one, which suits me fine.
Enriko: Convenient, that the one weapon nobody recognizes is extremely good for a trip where we might meet something big.
Lan (Smug): I like to think I got lucky.
label rockfangs
Enriko: Broken branch at chest height. Something big enough to shoulder through instead of going around. Claw drag, not paw.
Enriko: Rock Fang pack. Slow, stupid, mean when cornered. Perfect for beginners.
Liesel (Flat): You say that like you've done it before.
Enriko: I have not. I've read a great many books by people who have.
[signal arg="combat:rockfangs"]
Lan (Combat): (Longsword up. Take the lead one clean.)
Liesel (Default): Left flank, low.
Lan shifted without asking why, and felt claws rake past where his leg had been.
Lan (Smile): Nice call.
Liesel (Smug): I have eyes. And considerably more sense than either of you. You both walked into a pack formation like it was a straight line.
Enriko: In our defense, we're very stupid and very charming.
Liesel (Smile): One of those is true.
set {aff_liesel} += 1
Lan (Smile): (This is good. This is the part I actually get to keep.)
That was when the noise came in from the east. Not the clatter of Rock Fangs. The flat, human ring of steel on steel, and a scream.
Lan (Combat): That's not a monster fight.
label clearing
[signal arg="bg:forest_clearing"]
Lan (Talk): Liesel, stay with Enriko, hold this line.
Enriko: Already flaring it.
Leonora's party was down to her alone.
Both partners were on the ground and being dragged away, and six dark-clad attackers were closing a ring around her.
She fought with a single-edged arming sword, short economical cuts, and the ring kept shrinking.
Lan (Sus): (Three weeks of Amir's circulation drills. It still leaks at the edges, but for the first time there's a real current under the blade.)
The montante came off his back. Wide, continuous arcs forced the ring to open or lose limbs deciding not to.
The first attacker went down before he got close enough to touch Leonora.
Lan (Combat): (Pick the nearest. Corner him against the treeline. Then the next.)
[signal arg="combat:clearing_montante"]
It had been three weeks of careful, forgettable mediocrity. Something in him finally let out a breath.
His mouth curved into something that wasn't quite a smile.
Lan (Smug): (Just swing the sword until neither can.)
Leonora stood very still at his shoulder, blade still up, watching him cut through what was left of the ring.
The last of them broke and ran for the tree line. Lan let him go.
Chasing a runner alone into unfamiliar woods was exactly the overconfidence that got people killed in a story like this one.
Silence came down in pieces.
First the birds, then his own breathing, then the ordinary distant sound of other parties, entirely unaware anything had happened.
Leonora (Default): {rank}. You want to explain that?
Lan (Acting): Not really, no.
Lan (Sus): (Six men who came armed and organized to murder someone. Every rule I learned in either life says that puts them outside whatever mercy I have left.)
Lan (Sus): (I know who's behind it. Her brother.)
Lan (Sus): (Ambition dressed as restoring old glory, and a taste for solutions with no fingerprints.)
Lan (Sus): (If I say his name now with nothing but a rank {rank}'s word, I get killed quietly and the truth gets buried deeper.)
Lan (Sus): (So I say nothing. I file it beside the empty seat that used to be a hero.)
label word
Enriko: You hear about Al-Tale'a's side? Different part of the forest. Raiz's party got hit too.
Lan (Talk): Is he[pause=0.35][lspeed=0.25!]...[lspeed]
Enriko: Fine. More than fine. Word is he took a spear through the shoulder and a blade across the ribs and just kept walking.
Enriko: Let the wounds close mid-fight and used the time everyone else spent flinching.
Liesel (Flat): That's not normal regeneration. That's a body that doesn't register being outmatched as a reason to stop.
Enriko: Terrifying. Glad he's on nobody's enemy list. Well, nobody's official enemy list.
Lan (Sus): (Two royals. Two forests, opposite sides of the same class, the same day. Somebody wanted this to look like war.)
Lan (Sus): (And somebody's going to get blamed who didn't do it.)
[signal arg="chapter_end:ch04"]
